{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And all the souls.</b> He called seventy souls a single soul, to hint that there was peace among them, because there was no evil tongue and no informers among them — like a single person whose heart does not reveal what is in his mouth; so the matter was guarded among them all twelve months. And perhaps it is also for this reason that it says ״יֹצְאֵי יֶרֶךְ יַעֲקֹב״ — to tell you: just as the thigh is hidden, so among them too the matter was in secrecy."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:35.265230658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}